This science has been divided into two branches, natural and judiciary. To the former belongs the predicting of natural effects; as, the changes of weather, winds, storms, hurricanes, thunder, floods, earthquakes, &c. This art properly belongs to natural philosophy; and is only to be deduced, a posteriori, from phenomena and observations. Judiciary or judicial astrology, is that which pretends to foretell moral events; i.e. such as have a dependency on the free will and agency of man; as if they were directed by the stars. This art, which owed its origin to the practices of knavery on credulity, is now universally exploded by the intelligent part of mankind.

